        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "UNIT 5: VEHICLE CONSTRUCTIONS AND CONTROLS"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This chapter gives an overview of the light motor vehicle construction and controls. You will also learn where these parts are situated in the light vehicle and how they function. This is the control panel placed at the front of the vehicle or dashboard. The dashboard has instruments and controls used to run the vehicle.  You should get to know the names and location of these controls. You should also know how these controls and instruments function and how to maintain them. There are slight differences in the dashboard depending on the make and model of the vehicle. Below is a table indicating some of the components of a vehicle and their functions"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "Component"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "Function"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Steering Wheel This is used to change direction, or maintain the one you’re driving in. Both hands should be on the steering wheel at all times except to change gears or to indicate."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "[Figure/Diagram]"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Direction Indicator Used to indicate you wish to turn - signals turning left or right."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "[Figure/Diagram]"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Gear Lever Used to change gears."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "[Figure/Diagram]"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "Component"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "Function"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Hand Brake Used to keep your vehicle stationary, especially on inclines."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "[Figure/Diagram]"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Brake pedal Used to slow your speed or to stop"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "[Figure/Diagram]"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Accelerator Used to increase your speed."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "[Figure/Diagram]"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Clutch pedal Used to change gears in a manual vehicle"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "[Figure/Diagram]"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Rear-view Mirror Used to see other vehicles and hazards behind you for safety."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "[Figure/Diagram]"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
